{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>which he dreamed about them.</b> Concerning them; and he knew that they had been fulfilled, for behold — they bowed down to him." "<b>the nakedness of the land.</b> The exposure of the land — from where it is vulnerable to conquest, as in ״אֶת מְקֹרָהּ הֶעֱרָה״ (Leviticus 20), and like עֵרֹם וְעֶרְיָה (Ezekiel 16), and so every עֶרְוָה in Scripture is לשון exposure. And the Targum renders בִּדְקָא דְאַרְעָא, like בֶּדֶק הַבַּיִת (II Kings 12) — the shaking of the house; but it did not precise to explain it according to the language of Scripture."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:11.446042594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}